WEBVTT

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.730
NISHIKIZUTA HIGH SCHOOL

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.730
FLOWER FESTIVAL

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.900
EPISODE 06
WHEN I NEED
TO SAY SOMETHING,
I'LL SAY IT

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.240
<i>It's been one week.</i>

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.610
<i>Ever since that day,
I've barely had any contact with them.</i>

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.040
This is even worse than before we reconciled.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:46.750
<i>Additionally...</i>

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.630
If that article turns out to be true,
I'm going to make you pay!

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.340
<i>People still suspect me
of having three girlfriends.</i>

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:55.510
Yeah, whatever.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.170
Don't you get cocky with—

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.010
Joro! Good morning!

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.760
Huh? Am I interrupting?

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.310
It's nothing.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.480
You saved me, Asunaro.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.850
It's the least I could do!

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.320
<i>This past week,
she's the only one who's been by my side.</i>

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.740
<i>Thanks, Asunaro.</i>

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.280
What's wrong, Joro?

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.540
N-Nothing's wrong.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.040
Oh, that's right.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.420
The Flower Festival starts today, right?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.380
Are you worried
about what became of that article?

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.800
W-Well, maybe a little.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.380
Then, I'll answer you!

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.390
The article I wrote...

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.520
will be handed out on the second day
of the Flower Festival, so stay tuned.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.900
Not today?

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.560
Nope! Tomorrow!

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.230
So please do your best
with the Flower Dance today, Joro,

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.780
because I'll be cheering you on!

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.200
Okay. I will.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.330
TAIYO OGA

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.450
What's up, Sun-chan?

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.000
<i>Joro, we're in a real fix.</i>

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.830
A fix?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.750
PRINCIPAL' OFFICE

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.540
Yeah. I'm standing in front
of the principal's office right now.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.000
Listen to this.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.470
I heard there are two boys
performing at this year's Flower Dance!

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.140
<i>That's an important tradition!
What's the meaning of this?</i>

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.180
This is...

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.930
I guess the Flower Dance
is a hot-button topic among the PTA.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.730
They don't like the idea of two men being in it.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.150
Seriously?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.520
But why does it have to be on the day of?

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.650
<i>Sorry. I have a feeling
that I won't be allowed to participate.</i>

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.360
It's not your fault, Sun-chan!

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.780
<i>Anyway...</i>

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:49.660
Yeah. We can't cancel it,
so we need a girl to take my place.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.670
<i>Well, don't worry.
I'll solve this before you know it.</i>

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.130
Sun-chan!

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.880
Joro. About that...

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.760
Yeah. What a headache.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.510
A real mess.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.470
The Flower Dance is a really important event.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.640
If that's not held...

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.650
It's too early to throw in the towel.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.310
If we can find a substitute...

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.730
- Asunaro.
- Yes? What is it?

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.030
Would you take part in the dance?

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.660
Me?

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.250
Please! There's no one else I can ask!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.080
But...

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:32.910
Glance!

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.750
Just this once.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.670
Really? You're a lifesaver!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.090
Then, let's let President Cosmos
know right away!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.510
Yeah! Then—

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.590
That isn't necessary.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.390
Hi. Long time no see, you two.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.640
F-Feels like it has been a long time,
President Cosmos.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.520
Hello.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.860
I've been looking for you both,
but I didn't realize you were together.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.280
Oh, right!

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.940
About the Flower Dance member...

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:06.530
Are you going to say
that Asunaro will be the substitute?

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.240
Well, I asked her to do it.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.750
Not exactly what I expected.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.790
And you agreed, Asunaro?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:22.000
Yes, that's right.
When it comes to dancing, I'm not bad.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.720
I see. If we're that far into the scenario, then...

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.800
I don't believe
I have further business with Joro.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.520
Asunaro, would you come with me
to the Student Council Office?

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.850
Is this about the Flower Dance?

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.190
If so, then Joro should also—

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.650
There's no need.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.940
It's something that Joro shouldn't hear.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.620
If it's about the Flower Dance, then I'll go, too!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.200
- But...
- I also think Joro should go!

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.580
In fact, I'm not going without Joro!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.580
Are you sure?

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.840
Of course!

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:04.920
Okay.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.630
STUDENT COUNCIL OFFICE

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.970
So, Asunaro...

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.100
Yes.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.230
You agreed to participate
in the Flower Dance, right?

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:21.520
Yes. I thought all of you and Joro
were in trouble, so...

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.440
The way I was before,
I may not have been able to stop you.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.870
What does that...

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.120
Asunaro.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.830
I reject your participation in the Flower Dance.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.790
You're rejecting me?

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.920
What you should be doing right now

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:46.510
is putting together a newspaper
to retract your allegations about Joro

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.550
and delivering it to all the students.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:50.300
There's nothing else you need to do.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.550
Why do I have to sit here
and take that from you?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:58.680
I'm about to explain just why,
but I'll ask you one more time.

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.480
You're sure you don't mind Joro being here?

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.810
No, I don't mind!

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.770
<i>Hey, what is this?</i>

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.570
<i>Why is this happening?</i>

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.450
I see. Then—

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.320
But, first, there's one thing I need to check.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:16.370
You don't mind
if I quote you for an article, do you?

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:21.290
"The Student Council President's Tyranny!"
"Orders School Newspaper Content!"

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.250
That should be a good article.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.960
Do what you want.
I'm ready to accept that risk.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.430
But, Asunaro, after lying to everyone
and continuing to deceive Joro...

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.390
is that what you say?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.060
What? What are you talking about?

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.400
That's why I said Joro shouldn't hear this.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.950
Even though you knew
Joro didn't have three girlfriends,

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.610
you intentionally drove him into a corner.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:59.250
Despite boasting
of shadowing Joro for your story,

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.080
why did you stay away from the library

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.420
during the all-important lunch hour
when we would gather there?

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.380
I-I had to put together articles
in the newspaper office.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.590
Couldn't you have done that in the library?

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:15.680
I know what it is.
You had something else to do, didn't you?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.140
N-No, I didn't!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:23.100
I've confirmed it with students this past week,

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:28.820
but recently during lunch,
weird rumors about Joro go around.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.480
During lunch?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.780
Like rumors about Joro
having morally questionable interests.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.450
They mainly spread among the first-years.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.620
Apparently Kamata declined to take part
in the Flower Dance after hearing the rumors.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.620
<i>Go ahead!</i>

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.710
<i>Yes! I am the Slipper Man!</i>

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.880
That never happened! Don't distort reality!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:54.380
I've been workin' in the newspaper office
during lunch! I don't know anythin' about that!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.340
Then, let's move on.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.310
About a week ago, that article
about Joro got out in the form of an accident.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.560
The newspaper prints in the morning, and
for that day, the person in charge of the printing...

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.440
I didn't do the printin'! You can confirm that!

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.650
Of course. I already did.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.780
Then, you know I didn't do it!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:19.160
Yes. On the day it was printed, it was impossible
to replace one article with another.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.330
See?

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.790
But you did it the previous day after school.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.210
N-No.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:34.550
If you'd check
the printin' room key check-out sheet...

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:35.720
You mean this?

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:43.770
The person on duty that day...
wasn't Asunaro.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.770
YUKI ISHIKAWA

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.390
Th-There! That proves I didn't do it!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.440
Your biggest mistake was underestimating me.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.690
You altered this form.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.570
This is the real one, isn't it?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.540
H-How'd you get that?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.540
HINA HANETACHI

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.410
The morning that article about Joro
was accidentally passed out,

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:10.290
I already suspected you then,
so where do you think I went first?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.420
D-Don't tell me.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.880
Yes. The school newspaper's printing room.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.220
I believed you purposely
disseminated that article,

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:24.430
so I went to the printing room right away
and made a copy of the key check-out sheet.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.100
Then I took a gamble.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:33.150
I knew if I visited Joro's class
during that situation,

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.400
everyone would suspect me.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:39.280
Wait. You purposely brought up
the newspaper office so I'd...

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:41.700
<i>Joro.</i>

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:46.660
<i>I'll go to the newspaper office now
and order them to recall all the—</i>

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.750
<i>No need!</i>

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.920
<i>I'll take back all the copies myself right now!</i>

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.090
Thanks to that, I got it.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:59.090
Proof that there's no way
you can explain away.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:03.470
In other words, my gamble paid off.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:07.430
This issue over the Flower Dance, too,

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.690
the PTA president
confirmed who brought it up.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.070
Maybe if you had only gone
with one objective from the start,

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.490
your plan would have worked out, Asunaro.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.330
Only one objective?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.790
Your first objective was isolating Joro

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.920
to create an environment
in which only you could be at his side.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.710
But, when he was chosen
as a member of the Flower Dance,

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.380
you gained another objective.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.840
The objective for you yourself
to become a member of the dance.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.640
Why would you do that?

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.010
By doing that, she would obtain it.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.310
"The boy chosen to do the Flower Dance

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.730
always ends up marrying
one of the three chosen girls."

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.020
She wanted that bond with you, Joro.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.110
But I'm the one who asked Asunaro to do it—

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:05.660
This week, Asunaro is the only one
who's been practicing with you,

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.540
and you've been isolated.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.790
She was the only one
you could count on, right?

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.080
If you hadn't said anything,
she would've proposed it.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.630
Asunaro... you...

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.470
You're all... bein' unfair.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:26.930
It ain't fair!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.180
I always wanted to be with Joro!

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:32.310
But he's always with somebody else!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.100
It ain't fair!

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:40.480
Ever since the final game of the regional
baseball championship last summer,

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.950
I've been in love with Joro!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.990
I see. You, too, then.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.120
<i>I'm sorry, both of you.</i>

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.500
<i>I probably shouldn't go there,
but just allow me to say one thing.</i>

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.750
<i>God damn, you all love that one game!
How many times do we have to revisit that?</i>

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:05.010
That day, Joro protected me
from a stray foul ball.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.470
Nice ball!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:09.930
He was so cool.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.270
<i>Oh, that.</i>

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:17.230
<i>As I recall, I was just moving to get
a better look at some beautiful girl with big tits.</i>

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:21.280
So it should just be me!
It should just be me an' Joro!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.400
Joro doesn't need any buddies!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.990
You should all get lost!

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.990
Asunaro, you're asking for the impossible.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.240
- That ain't true! It ain't.
- It is.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.870
No matter who you drag down
so you're the last one standing,

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:38.330
you won't obtain what you really want.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:43.340
True love is difficult.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:48.180
In my own experience, I was so selfish
that it brought him nothing but trouble,

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.180
and it ended up going nowhere.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:56.190
The idea that effort will always be rewarded,
when applied to love, is just a lie.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.230
I'm sure being unrewarded
is much more common.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:08.780
But I think that, when it is rewarded,
when you do get there, the joy is immeasurable.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.910
So what are you going to do now, Asunaro?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.670
Joro...

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.630
I-I really do love you!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:29.220
So please let me be with you
more than anyone else!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.350
I'm sorry, Asunaro.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:39.100
I don't have any romantic feelings for you.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.520
And what the hell did you do?

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.570
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.610
B-But I love—

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.950
Shut up! Forget about me!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.870
Do you know how much trouble
you've caused Sun-chan?

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.830
He gave up precious baseball practice
to rehearse for the dance!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.330
And the others, too!

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:11.140
You'll never be by my side again,
and you can take that to the bank.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.010
That's all.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:17.930
I see.

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:23.770
President Cosmos. I apologize
for all of the trouble I've caused.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.570
I'll do everything you said.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.990
Can I have faith in your word?

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:33.240
Yes! Because the school newspaper
reveals the truth!

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.870
Thank you, Asunaro.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:40.000
Well, I have a new newspaper
to put together, so I'll be on my way.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.210
Excuse me!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.090
I lost.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.590
You really are insensitive and cruel.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:54.720
That's right! That's the kind of bastard I am!

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.680
Or that's what you want me to say, right?

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:02.100
You acted like an insufferable jerk
to give her a push.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.560
Of course you're not insensitive and cruel.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.900
You're rough around the edges,
but I think you're very kind.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:13.910
You're putting way too much...
Er, you're overestimating me.

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:16.490
The way you were was fine.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.910
Anyway, what about the Flower Dance?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.160
- At this rate...
- We don't need a substitute.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:27.460
The Flower Dance is an event
with one boy and three girls.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:31.590
No matter how many members we're short,
we're not going to have another boy.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:36.300
"I'm going to convince her!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:40.430
I'm sure Joro
wants to do the Flower Dance with her!"

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:42.850
That's what Sun-chan told me.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.650
So Himawari and I
have been cooperating with him.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.480
"Her"?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.280
Himawari, Sun-chan, and I
have wanted to make it up to you.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.280
Even if you have already
forgiven us for before...

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.620
Y-You don't mean...

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.000
Speak of the devil, I guess?

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.600
FLOWER FESTIVAL
FLOWER DANCE

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.350
What do you think? I'm good, right?

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.070
H-Hey, don't be so rough.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.320
I can't hear you!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.740
Hey, Joro.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:35.780
What?

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.870
Do you have a crush on anyone now?

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:38.780
No.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.450
Oh.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.870
Then, that makes two of us.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.340
That was beautiful, Himawari!

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:51.920
That dress really looks good on you!

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.720
- President Cosmos!
- I've been waiting for you!

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.010
Don't stand up!
I could barely see when you were sitting!

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.480
Well, ready to give it a whirl?

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:35.970
You don't have to worry on Asunaro's behalf.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.130
What do you mean?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:42.470
Only you, Sun-chan,
and I know about her secret.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.100
All right.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.570
GET THAT SCOOP!!

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:57.700
Thank you for everything that you've done,
President Cosmos.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.160
I'm the one who should be thanking you.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.740
Because of you, the Flower Dance
has gone without a hitch.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.290
She agreed to do it
because you were participating.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.340
President Cosmos, that was awesome!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.470
So I'll give you a reward.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.050
What kind of reward?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.050
This kind of reward.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.470
One week...

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:30.690
I missed you more than anyone.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.310
Well, I'm out of here!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.900
Did that happen?

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:52.170
Shall we dance?

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.130
What's wrong, Joro?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.630
Y-Yeah.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:00.840
Who is that girl?

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:01.970
I don't know.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:05.510
- She's gorgeous.
- Maybe she's a new student?

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:06.720
I've never seen her before.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.930
This is bad.
Too much chatter from the audience.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:11.940
I just hope they don't get distracted.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:24.450
Joro and Pansy are so elegant!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.620
Yeah.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.410
Joro.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:33.830
Am I pretty?

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:37.130
A Japanese person doesn't compliment
another on their Japanese.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.340
Thank you.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:44.220
Say, can I ask you something?

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.050
What is it?

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:49.270
Why did you put someone else
before yourself again this time?

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:54.020
FLOWER FESTIVAL
FLOWER DANCE

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:51.480
What are you talking about?

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:54.020
You tried to get me to make friends,
didn't you?

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:58.020
It started at the midterm study session.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:03.820
You held it in the library
to break the ice between me and them.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:07.320
After that, it was lunchtime in the library.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.540
AMATSUYU KISARAGI
PURE PURITY PLAN

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:11.830
You had everyone gather there
for a strategy session.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:16.080
So why did you go
through all that trouble for my sake?

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.590
- Because I'm grateful to you.
- Grateful?

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:29.430
I was moved that you helped me
when I was in a bind at school,

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.430
so I was grateful!

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.390
That's why I wanted to pay you back!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:36.520
Oh.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.940
I'll tell you the meaning of Western pansies
in the language of flowers.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.200
Yellow pansies mean memories.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.410
White pansies mean the feeling of love.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:50.370
And purple pansies mean...

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.250
my head is filled with thoughts of you.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:07.380
With the legend of the Flower Dance in mind,
it's possible that we'll get married tomorrow.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:11.810
Unfortunately, it seems
that legend won't apply this year.

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:15.600
I'm half sad and half relieved.

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:17.520
Pansy, you were beautiful out there!

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:20.400
My heart was beating fast
the whole time I watched you!

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.570
Thank you, Pansy.
The Flower Dance was a great success.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:25.110
That's good to hear.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:26.860
You, too, Joro. Good job!

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:29.490
Sun-chan, I can't believe you!

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:31.910
I told you at the beginning!

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:33.990
There was something else I had to do!

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:35.750
This was it!

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:37.750
Is that right?

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:39.120
Well...

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:40.790
thanks.

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:49.220
Um, do you mind if I say one more thing?

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:52.600
Wh-What is it, Sanshokuin?

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:57.480
Today's Flower Dance, um, it was a lot of fun.

00:22:58.100 --> 00:22:58.940
So...

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:03.020
I hope to see more of you...

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:04.480
Himawari...

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:06.030
Cosmos...

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:07.190
Sun-chan.

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:13.870
Sure! Even after this, we're friends, Pansy!

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:16.910
Good. I feel the same way.

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:20.710
I'm looking forward to seeing more of you too,
Pansy, but I'm not going to lose.

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:22.840
That's my line.

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:25.590
You'll be seeing more of me, too, Pansy.

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:27.300
Joro.

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:28.670
What?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:32.680
Well? We've got lovely friends, don't we?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
EPISODE 07
I DISCOVER AN UNEXPECTED SIDE.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.810
I Discover an Unexpected Side
